          "color": "ink",
          "align": "justify",
          "cols": 1,
          "text": "<span class='sc'>Turning Point</span> is an installation project by Anant National University, created for the India Art Biennale 2026.",
          "sel": ".frame > .intro",
          "id": "e4i79",
          "textFrom": "<span class='sc'>Turning Point</span> is an installation project by Anant National University, created for the India Art Biennale 2026."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Intro text",
          "x": 6.25,
          "y": 3.5,
          "w": 4,
          "h": 4.5,
          "font": "text",
          "size": 0.205,
          "lh": 1.3,
          "color": "ink",
          "align": "justify",
          "cols": 1,
          "text": "At its core is a physical structure made of four spiraling steel columns that are held together in dynamic balance. Each 6 meter tall column rotates gradually from the base and is imbricated with patterns of emergent life-processes.\n\nThe work invites you to examine the site through these perforations, pondering our relationships with the self, the other and the cosmos at large.\n\nYou can <a data-go='explore'>explore</a> interactive interpretations of the site and its themes, read more about the <a data-go='structure'>structure</a> and its construction, see upcoming <a data-go='events'>events</a>, or find out about the <a data-go='credits'>team</a> that built the project.",
          "sel": ".intro p",
          "id": "e5j8x",
          "textFrom": "At its core is a physical structure made of four spiraling steel columns that are held together in dynamic balance. Each 6 meter tall column rotates gradually from the base and is imbricated with patterns of emergent life-processes.\n\nThe work invites you to examine the site through these perforations, pondering our relationships with the self, the other and the cosmos at large.\n\nYou can <a data-go='explore'>explore</a> interactive interpretations of the site and its themes, read more about the <a data-go='structure'>structure</a> and its construction, see upcoming <a data-go='events'>events</a>, or find out about the <a data-go='credits'>team</a> that built the project."
